member.summary:
Resolves the Apply method for a runtime event instance type. Exact CLR-type identity is tried first
so this entry point cannot return  where the name-based one would throw;
otherwise a caller that silently skips unresolved events would drop the event without a diagnostic.

member.remarks:
Uses independent finite discovery admission held until actual provider completion. An outstanding
            provider/store/scope/key is refused on repeated scans, including through a reconstructed coordinator;
            late results are discarded and every subsequent admitted read validates fresh offboarding evidence.

Generalizes the per-domain consumer contexts domain modules previously hand-wrote (e.g.
TenantEventContext). Identifier fields are compared case-sensitively (Ordinal) by convention;
canonical casing is the publisher's responsibility.

